<?xml version="1.0"?>
<rdf:RDF xmlns="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/oheo#"
     xml:base="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/oheo"
     xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"
     xmlns:ns1="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/oheo/"
     xmlns:obo="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/"
     xmlns:owl="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#"
     xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#"
     xmlns:xml="http://www.w3.org/XML/1998/namespace"
     xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#"
     xmlns:foaf="http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/"
     xmlns:rdfs="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#"
     xmlns:rheo="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/rheo/"
     xmlns:skos="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#"
     xmlns:vann="http://purl.org/vocab/vann/"
     xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/"
     xmlns:oboInOwl="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#">
    <owl:Ontology rdf:about="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/oheo">
        <owl:versionIRI rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/oheo/0.3.0/oheo.owl"/>
        <dcterms:bibliographicCitation>Baines D, Ashley M. Outcomes Health Economics Ontology (OHEO), version 0.2.0. Intelligent Parameters Ltd; 2026. https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/oheo/0.3.0/oheo.owl. Licence CC BY 4.0.</dcterms:bibliographicCitation>
        <dcterms:created>2026-10-08</dcterms:created>
        <dcterms:creator rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9502-4678"/>
        <dcterms:creator rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0009-0006-0231-3731"/>
        <dcterms:description xml:lang="en">An ontology of health outcomes as they are specified, measured, valued and summarised for health economics and health technology assessment. OHEO keeps four kinds of thing apart: outcome domains (what is measured, aligned to the 38 domains of the COMET outcome taxonomy), outcome measurement instruments (how it is measured; each named instrument is a class whose instances are its versions), valuations (utility functions and value sets, each named value set a class whose instances are its releases), and summary measures (QALY, DALY and related estimates). Outcome specifications, records of individual measurements, valuation methods and the reference cases of decision-making bodies are described with them. Policy (agreed with Darrin Baines, 15 October 2026): HEO identifies concepts; RHEO and OHEO define types classified within BFO 2020 (ISO/IEC 21838-2). A concept and a type have different identifiers even when their names are alike, and no OHEO class uses a HEO concept URI. HEO is the thesaurus of concepts; RHEO and OHEO classify kinds of things and do not overlap where they are used operationally (OHEO declares its records disjoint from the RHEO records they sit beside). SKOS names broker between them: the mappings to HEO concepts and RHEO types are published in oheo-mappings.sssom.tsv with justified, non-exact predicates, and a mapping never states identity. Requirements that records and analyses must meet, including the reference cases of NICE and nine other bodies, are published as SHACL shapes (oheo-shapes.ttl and oheo-reference-case-shapes.ttl), because OWL&apos;s open-world semantics cannot treat missing information as an error.</dcterms:description>
        <dcterms:issued>2026-10-16</dcterms:issued>
        <dcterms:license rdf:resource="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"/>
        <dcterms:modified>2026-10-16</dcterms:modified>
        <dcterms:publisher>Intelligent Parameters Ltd</dcterms:publisher>
        <dcterms:subject>COMET</dcterms:subject>
        <dcterms:subject>COSMIN</dcterms:subject>
        <dcterms:subject>QALY</dcterms:subject>
        <dcterms:subject>core outcome sets</dcterms:subject>
        <dcterms:subject>health economics</dcterms:subject>
        <dcterms:subject>health outcomes</dcterms:subject>
        <dcterms:subject>health technology assessment</dcterms:subject>
        <dcterms:subject>health utility</dcterms:subject>
        <dcterms:subject>outcome measurement</dcterms:subject>
        <dcterms:subject>patient-reported outcome measures</dcterms:subject>
        <dcterms:title xml:lang="en">Outcomes Health Economics Ontology (OHEO)</dcterms:title>
        <vann:preferredNamespacePrefix>oheo</vann:preferredNamespacePrefix>
        <vann:preferredNamespaceUri>https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/oheo/OHEO_</vann:preferredNamespaceUri>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Pre-1.0 release (status alpha) for review by its creators and invited reviewers; terms, definitions and mappings may still change before version 1.0. OHEO imports RHEO 0.4.0, which imports BFO 2020; the BFO, IAO, OBI, COB and STATO terms that RHEO declares are not declared again here. Other reused terms (from IAO, OBI, STATO, OGMS and OAE) are declared with their official label and definition as served by the EBI Ontology Lookup Service on 16 October 2026, with one of their source-asserted parents; consult the source ontologies for their full axioms.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment>OHEO 0.3.0 merged with its imports (RHEO 0.4.0 and BFO 2020) into one file for BioPortal and other tools that cannot resolve the import IRIs. Built by run_demo.py with ROBOT merge.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heo"/>
        <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/rheo"/>
        <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/subdomain/outcomes"/>
        <owl:versionInfo>0.3.0 (alpha)</owl:versionInfo>
        <foaf:homepage rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/oheo"/>
    </owl:Ontology>
    


